## 2. Frozen 12-Table Schema Specifications

1. **`roles`**: `id` (PK), `name` (UNIQUE), `description`, `created_at`. Seed values: `admin`, `accountant`, `manager`, `viewer`.
2. **`users`**: `id` (PK), `role_id` (FK ➔ `roles.id`), `name`, `email` (UNIQUE), `password_hash`, `status`, `last_login_at`, `created_at`, `updated_at`.
3. **`companies`**: `id` (PK), `company_name`, `registration_number` (UNIQUE), `email`, `phone`, `address`, `industry`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`.
4. **`loans`**: `id` (PK), `company_id` (FK ➔ `companies.id`), `loan_number` (UNIQUE), `principal_amount`, `interest_rate`, `total_payable`, `start_date`, `end_date`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`.
5. **`repayment_schedules`**: `id` (PK), `loan_id` (FK ➔ `loans.id`), `installment_number`, `due_date`, `principal_due`, `interest_due`, `total_due`, `amount_paid`, `amount_pending`, `status`, UNIQUE(`loan_id`, `installment_number`), `created_at`, `updated_at`.
6. **`payments`**: `id` (PK), `payment_reference` (UNIQUE), `transaction_reference` (UNIQUE), `payment_date`, `amount`, `payment_method`, `bank_reference`, `sender_name`, `sender_account`, `raw_description`, `source`, `status` (`unmatched`, `under_review`, `matched`, `partially_allocated`, `fully_allocated`, `rejected`), `created_at`, `updated_at`.
7. **`reconciliation_cases`**: `id` (PK), `payment_id` (FK ➔ `payments.id`), `status` (`pending`, `ai_analyzing`, `ai_recommended`, `under_review`, `approved`, `rejected`, `resolved`), `priority`, `assigned_to` (FK ➔ `users.id`, nullable), `matched_company_id` (FK ➔ `companies.id`, nullable), `matched_loan_id` (FK ➔ `loans.id`, nullable), `matched_repayment_id` (FK ➔ `repayment_schedules.id`, nullable), `created_at`, `resolved_at`.
8. **`ai_recommendations`**: `id` (PK), `reconciliation_case_id` (FK ➔ `reconciliation_cases.id`), `agent_name`, `recommended_company_id` (FK ➔ `companies.id`, nullable), `recommended_loan_id` (FK ➔ `loans.id`, nullable), `recommended_repayment_id` (FK ➔ `repayment_schedules.id`, nullable), `recommended_amount`, `confidence_score`, `reasoning_summary`, `status` (`pending`, `approved`, `rejected`), `reviewed_by` (FK ➔ `users.id`, nullable), `reviewed_at`, `created_at`.
9. **`payment_allocations`**: `id` (PK), `payment_id` (FK ➔ `payments.id`), `repayment_schedule_id` (FK ➔ `repayment_schedules.id`), `allocated_amount`, `allocation_type` (`full`, `partial`, `overpayment`, `manual`, `ai_recommended`), `approved_by` (FK ➔ `users.id`), `approved_at`, `created_at`.
10. **`documents`**: `id` (PK), `company_id` (FK ➔ `companies.id`), `loan_id` (FK ➔ `loans.id`, nullable), `document_type`, `file_name`, `file_url`, `mime_type`, `file_size`, `uploaded_by` (FK ➔ `users.id`), `approved_by` (FK ➔ `users.id`, nullable), `approved_at`, `status`, `created_at`.
11. **`audit_logs`**: `id` (PK BIGINT), `user_id` (FK ➔ `users.id`, nullable), `action`, `entity_type`, `entity_id`, `old_value` (JSON), `new_value` (JSON), `ip_address`, `created_at`.
12. **`notifications`**: `id` (PK BIGINT), `user_id` (FK ➔ `users.id`), `type`, `title`, `message`, `reference_type`, `reference_id`, `is_read`, `created_at`.

